description:
Found 2026-09-20 while making the payment-channel seam production-ready (V-110/V-111 pass).

payment_channel_manager_actor.dart, _spendFundingInputs:
  Future<Set<String>?> unspentKeys() async { ... storage.getUTXOs(walletId) ... }
  final unspent = await unspentKeys();
  for (final input in funding.inputs) {
    if (unspent != null && !unspent.contains(key)) continue;

The question asked is 'is this input still unspent?'. An EMPTY answer therefore means 'everything is already spent', so a read model that knows NOTHING makes this skip every SpendUTXOCommand. Absence of knowledge is being read as evidence of a spend - the exact inversion this backlog keeps finding (V-102's _fundingHoldReleased got this right: 'an absent record never refuses').

Reachable in production, not only in tests: the read model lags the journal (the reason WalletSpendableUtxosQuery exists at all), so a funding broadcast whose inputs have not yet been projected skips their spends. The same inversion is in the second use a few lines below: notApplied.retainWhere(unspentNow.contains).

FIX: ask the positive question. Collect the keys the read model shows SPENT (getUTXOs(walletId, includeSpent: true) filtered on UTXOStatus.spent) and skip only those; an input the read model does not vouch for still gets its command, which the wallet refuses harmlessly if it was spent after all. Change retainWhere to removeWhere on the spent set.

WHY IT IS NOT FIXED YET - this is the blocker and it is shared with libspiffy-m0xj. The change was written and reverted because NO TEST CAN REACH _spendFundingInputs with a read model present:
 - it runs only after a successful funding broadcast (call site ~1772), and the funding BEEF is built before the broadcast in the same method;
 - _buildFundingBeef needs the funding's ancestors, with a merkle proof, in the read model;
 - ChannelRefundFixture's funding spends a SYNTHETIC parent (c0c0...) that has no transaction to store, so with a storage present the open always fails with 'Cannot build the BEEF' - which two existing tests already assert (payment_channel_manager_funding_test.dart:276, and the repair/alice-bob tests fail this way if storage is supplied).

So the prerequisite is fixture work: give ChannelRefundFixture (or a sibling) a funding transaction with a REAL provable parent, using the recipe in test/services/ancestor_chain_beef_order_test.dart:84-108 (store the ancestor transactions, store a merkle proof for the root, store the block header). channelFundingWithBeef in test/actors/channel_test_fixtures.dart already builds a funding with a real parent and a BEEF and is the obvious starting point.

That one piece of fixture work unblocks THREE things: this fix, libspiffy-m0xj (making storage required, which today breaks payment_channel_repair_test and alice_bob_cqrs_channel_test for exactly this reason), and storage-backed integration coverage of the funding path generally.

A NOTE comment naming this bead is in the code at the unspentKeys() doc so a reader does not have to rediscover it.
